::ENG3_U05_L04_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.V.03] Context: The writer gently offers one possible answer instead of demanding agreement. Which word best fits this meaning? {
~commands#Incorrect. "Commands" means orders, which is too forceful.
~guesses#Incorrect. "Guesses" suggests uncertainty without support.
=suggests#Correct. "Suggests" means offers an idea for consideration.
~ignores#Incorrect. "Ignores" means pays no attention.
}

::ENG3_U05_L04_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: credible, credit, credential. The root idea relates to belief or trust. What does "credible" most nearly mean? {
~Expensive.#Incorrect. The word family does not point to cost.
=Believable.#Correct. "Credible" means able to be believed or trusted.
~Invisible.#Incorrect. The root clue does not relate to sight.
~Temporary.#Incorrect. The word family does not point to time.
}

::ENG3_U05_L04_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.V.03] Reference entry: concise means "using few words while still being clear." Which sentence uses "concise" correctly? {
=The editor praised the concise summary because it explained the issue in two clear sentences.#Correct. The summary is brief and clear.
~The concise speech lasted four hours and repeated every point.#Incorrect. Long and repetitive is not concise.
~The concise hallway was painted blue.#Incorrect. "Concise" describes expression, not a hallway.
~The concise storm flooded the road.#Incorrect. The word does not describe weather.
}

::ENG3_U05_L04_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Source sentence: The council delayed the vote until members could review the budget more carefully. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
~The council voted against the budget after refusing to read it.#Incorrect. The source says the vote was delayed, not rejected.
~The council approved the budget without discussion.#Incorrect. This reverses the action.
~The budget was canceled because members disliked it.#Incorrect. The source does not say the budget was canceled.
=The council postponed the vote so members could examine the budget in more detail.#Correct. This keeps the meaning while changing the wording.
}

::ENG3_U05_L04_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.V.03] Context: A student needs the exact pronunciation and part of speech for "articulate." Which reference material is most useful? {
~An atlas.#Incorrect. An atlas provides maps, not pronunciation or part of speech.
~A timeline.#Incorrect. A timeline shows events in order.
=A dictionary entry.#Correct. A dictionary gives pronunciation, part of speech, definitions, and usage.
~A weather chart.#Incorrect. A weather chart does not explain word meaning.
}
